==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|absterse}}, from {{der|en|la|abstersus}}, perfect passive participle of {{m|la|abstergeō||wipe off, wipe away}}; formed from {{m|la|abs-}} + {{m|la|tergeō||wipe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əbˈstɜː(ɹ)s/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/æbˈstɝs/|/əbˈstɝs/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-absterse.wav|a=US}}
* {{hyphenation|en|ab|sterse}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)s|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|now|rare}} To [[absterge]]; to [[cleanse]]; to [[purge]] away. {{defdate|First attested around 1350 to 1470.}}<ref name=SOED>{{R:SOED5|page=10}}</ref>
#* {{RQ:Browne Pseudodoxia Epidemica|chapter=Of the Oestridge|page=164|passage={{...}} nor will we affirme that Iron ingeſted, receiveth in the ſtomack of the Oeſtridge no alteration whatſoever; but if any ſuch there be, we ſuſpect this effect rather from ſome way of corroſion, then any of digeſtion; not any liquid reduction or tendance to chilification by the power of naturall heate, but rather ſome attrition from an acide and vitriolous humidity in the ſtomack, which may '''abſterſe''', and ſhave the ſcorious parts thereof; {{...}}}}

